@startuml f10-cleanup-scope-expires
title F10 — Container cleanup and scope expiry

|EX|
start
:Terminal event received
 (any of: F8 final, F7 cancel,
 F9 cancel, F6 timeout);

:Stop container process
 (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after grace);

:Mount tmpfs cleanup
 (/run/secrets/* unmounted);

note right
  Plaintext bytes gone the moment
  the unmount completes.
end note

:Notify EX of container exit;
:Update internal task state;
:Release executor slot;

|Secret Registry|
:Scope_token still valid until TTL;
:No action on Secret Registry side at cleanup time;
:Plaintext already gone from container;
:TTL countdown continues;
:When TTL = 0, signature invalidated;
:Future get-by-scope with this scope
 fails closed;

note right
  Secret Registry does NOT need to know about cleanup.
  It just enforces TTL on every request.
end note

|State Registry|
:Audit log already persisted
 (during F8 or F9);
:State Registry keeps:
 status, event log, audit;
:Plaintext NEVER enters State Registry;

stop

note right
  Container terminated -> tmpfs unmount ->
  plaintext gone -> scope expires ->
  State Registry keeps audit and task history only.
end note

@enduml
